From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:53:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] class expression: accept contextual keywords as class names

A class name is a BindingIdentifier, and contextual keywords such as
`of`, `async`, `get` and `set` are valid ones. 0.22 accepts them in
class declarations, but the class expression parser still forwards
only plain identifiers and yield/await. Minified bundles reuse short
names such as `of` freely, and one such class expression makes the
whole script fail with "expected class identifier".

Forward every keyword except `extends` to BindingIdentifier, with
upstream's is_reserved_identifier rule, so reserved words are still
rejected.
---
 src/parser/expression/primary/class_expression/mod.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/parser/expression/primary/class_expression/mod.rs b/src/parser/expression/primary/class_expression/mod.rs
index 417eede..3d13ce5 100644
--- a/src/parser/expression/primary/class_expression/mod.rs
+++ b/src/parser/expression/primary/class_expression/mod.rs
@@ -62,6 +62,13 @@ where
                     .parse(cursor, interner)?
                     .into()
             }
+            // Same contextual-keyword rule as class declarations (`class of extends X`);
+            // BindingIdentifier still rejects the reserved words.
+            TokenKind::Keyword((k, _)) if !k.to_sym().is_reserved_identifier() => {
+                BindingIdentifier::new(self.allow_yield, self.allow_await)
+                    .parse(cursor, interner)?
+                    .into()
+            }
             _ => None,
         };
         cursor.set_strict(strict);
